is, but constitutional symptoms and leukemoid reaction suggest a more complex systemic process", "Malignancy with bone metastases: Weight loss and hypercalcemia are concerning, but lacks specific neurologic or visceral localization", "Vitamin D toxicity: On vitamin D supplementation, but would typically show more pronounced renal impairment (BUN/Creatinine ratio is normal here)", "Acute leukemia: Leukocytosis with elevated LAP points against CML, but myeloproliferative disorders remain possible", "Severe infection: Leukemoid reaction might suggest infection, but no fever or other septic markers present"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss", "Hypercalcemia", "Leukocytosis with elevated LAP"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.062316847151914274, "posterior": 0.06342342015284703, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and hypercalcemia weakly contradict reactive leukemoid reaction (B5) and slightly support malignant processes."], "evidence_against": ["Hypercalcemia without marrow fibrosis or blast crisis weakly contradicts CML (B3.1) but does not decisively confirm plasma cell disorders (B4)."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.001, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Hypercalcemia without marrow fibrosis or blast crisis weakly contradicts CML (B3.1) but does not