e novo AML (B1.1) as a dangerous differential within Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts (B1)?", "summary": "The absence of marrow fibrosis or blast crisis features in the physical exam does not rule out de novo AML (B1.1) as a dangerous differential. Elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase (LAP) and constitutional symptoms (weight loss, fatigue) with hypercalcemia provide weak support for CML (B3.1) whil…"}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.374], ["B3.1", 0.303], ["B4", 0.108]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.485], ["B3.1", 0.439], ["B4", 0.083]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.346], ["B3.1", 0.306], ["B1", 0.062]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers present. Vital signs are non-critical (mild hypertension, tachycardia without end-organ signs, normal oxygenation). Leukocytosis with elevated LAP suggests a leukemoid reaction rather than CML or other acute hematologic emergencies requiring urgent intervention.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch B3.1 (CML) has posterior 0.306 (<0.75 threshold). Dangerous alternatives (B1.1 AML with danger=0.8) remain unresolved but do not meet posterior ≥0.10 threshold. Untried discriminators like bone marrow biopsy or cytogenetic testing could refine diagnosis."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.5, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.30643991521431063, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic lymphoma"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic myeloid leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Leukemoid reaction"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phe